@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
    ViewData["Description"] = "What ZapWatch collects, which third parties process it, and how to request deletion.";
}

<p class="zw-eyebrow mb-1">Privacy Policy</p>
<h1 class="mb-4">Privacy Policy</h1>

<div class="zw-card p-4 p-md-5" style="max-width:760px;">
    <p class="zw-muted mb-4" style="font-size:0.9rem;">
        <strong class="text-body">This is a starter draft written to accurately describe what
        ZapWatch actually does today &mdash; it is not legal advice.</strong> If you're relying on
        this for compliance purposes, have it reviewed by someone qualified first.
    </p>

    <h3>What we collect</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Account info:</strong> your email address, and your phone number if you add one
            (used only to send SMS alerts).</li>
        <li><strong>Automation data:</strong> the names you give your monitored automations, their
            expected-frequency and grace-period settings, and the timestamp of every ping received
            at your automations' unique ping URLs.</li>
        <li><strong>Alert history:</strong> when an automation went overdue, when it recovered,
            which channels (email/SMS) were notified, and details of any failed send.</li>
        <li><strong>Billing status:</strong> your plan, subscription status, and Razorpay
            subscription ID. We never see or store your card details &mdash; those go directly to
            Razorpay.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="zw-muted" style="font-size:0.9rem;">
        We don't see the contents of the Zaps you're monitoring &mdash; only that a ping arrived
        and when. The "Webhooks by Zapier" step you add per the <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Onboarding">onboarding guide</a>
        doesn't need to send us any of your Zap's actual data.
    </p>

    <h3>Third parties that process your data</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Razorpay</strong> &mdash; processes your payment when you subscribe. Handles
            your card/payment details directly; we only receive a subscription ID and status.</li>
        <li><strong>Twilio</strong> (SMS alerts during build/early operation; migrating to an
            India-focused provider such as MSG91 once live, per our own build notes) &mdash; sends
            the SMS alert text and your phone number to deliver it.</li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong> &mdash; sends transactional email: alerts, signup verification,
            and password reset links. Receives your email address and the message content.</li>
        <li><strong>Google</strong> &mdash; if you choose "Continue with Google" to sign in, Google
            shares your email address with us to match or create your account. We don't request
            access to anything else in your Google account.</li>
        <li><strong>MonsterASP.NET</strong> &mdash; our hosting provider. All application data,
            including the database described above, lives on their infrastructure.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>How long we keep it</h3>
    <p>
        Account, automation, ping, and alert data is kept for as long as your account is active.
        There's no automatic deletion job running yet for old ping/alert history &mdash; we intend
        to add a rolling retention window for that data, but as of today it's retained
        indefinitely alongside the rest of your account. Deleting an automation from your
        dashboard immediately deletes its ping and alert history along with it.
    </p>

    <h3>Your rights / requesting deletion</h3>
    <p>
        There's no self-serve "delete my account" button yet. To request deletion of your account
        and all associated data, email us at
        <a href="mailto:iamanseernk@gmail.com">iamanseernk@gmail.com</a> from the address on your
        account and we'll delete it manually. We'll confirm once it's done.
    </p>

    <h3>Changes to this policy</h3>
    <p class="mb-0">
        If what we collect or who we share it with changes, we'll update this page. Check back
        periodically if that matters to you.
    </p>
</div>
